{"h":3395,"lines":[{"x":0.79178354908764093,"y":0.1007270089152994,"c":1,"t":"Reading","w":0.079038976033528607,"h":0.015990422387005099},{"t":"Around this time, Moore moved away from the human figure to experiment with abstract shapes.","w":0.77160491943359366,"h":0.016017476296396826,"x":0.088477375565440095,"y":0.14534883706336088,"c":1},{"h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1,"x":0.088477377510026822,"t":"In 1931, he held an exhibition at the Leicester Galleries in London. His work was enthusiastically","y":0.16133720952043984,"w":0.77777776082356775},{"x":0.088477378399860529,"t":"welcomed by fellow sculptors, but the reviews in the press were extremely negative and turned","w":0.75308639526367194,"h":0.016027748233718775,"c":1,"y":0.17873969376817755},{"c":1,"x":0.088398244724879754,"h":0.018668538690034597,"t":"Moore into a notorious figure. There were calls for his resignation from the Royal College,","y":0.19356980986074901,"w":0.72444468180338539},{"w":0.74912867228190105,"c":1,"y":0.2103925234244628,"h":0.0209361010080793,"t":"and the following year, when his contract expired, he left to start a sculpture department at the","x":0.088394750842641756},{"h":0.018190073882733082,"t":"Chelsea School of Art in London.","w":0.27216389973958333,"y":0.22610950180681988,"x":0.088251876611467564,"c":1},{"y":0.26148409914536086,"x":0.088477365889965451,"c":1,"t":"Throughout the 1930s, Moore did not show any inclination to please the British public. He","w":0.72427983601888024,"h":0.016195524146054074},{"y":0.27906976729598143,"w":0.76131688435872391,"c":1,"t":"became interested in the paintings of the Spanish artist Pablo Picasso, whose work inspired him","h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.088477360184909148},{"y":0.2950530037009389,"h":0.015993508068214979,"t":"to distort the human body in a radical way. At times, he seemed to abandon the human figure","w":0.74279836018880208,"c":1,"x":0.08641974984199427},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"y":0.3124263838351331,"t":"altogether. The pages of his sketchbooks from this period show his ideas for abstract sculptures","w":0.75925923665364581,"x":0.08847737744843262},{"t":"that bore little resemblance to the human form.","c":1,"h":0.016119222899348307,"x":0.088338433093592059,"w":0.37683146158854164,"y":0.32797620761785984},{"h":0.016010628150966877,"w":0.78189300537109363,"t":"In 1940, during the Second World War, Moore stopped teaching at the Chelsea School and moved","c":1,"x":0.086419752355605409,"y":0.36189634873478105},{"y":0.37735390717584805,"t":"to a farmhouse about 20 miles north of London. A shortage of materials forced him to focus","w":0.73880299886067702,"h":0.017877144583262838,"c":1,"x":0.086362049842199154},{"y":0.39534883704983015,"h":0.017489796673310742,"t":"on drawing. He did numerous small sketches of Londoners, later turning these ideas into large","c":1,"x":0.088477378390197897,"w":0.75308639526367194},{"y":0.41131735248561141,"h":0.019550561624084417,"c":1,"w":0.7820074971516926,"t":"coloured drawings in his studio. In 1942, he returned to Castleford to make a series of sketches of","x":0.08843254201735079},{"y":0.42621228209416229,"h":0.017242738299150906,"x":0.090261628717847014,"w":0.2393364715576172,"c":1,"t":"the miners who worked there."},{"h":0.016000356213644817,"y":0.46220930217960743,"x":0.088477372114381586,"w":0.73868311564127609,"t":"In 1944, Harlow, a town near London, offered Moore a commission for a sculpture depicting","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.088477360493101759,"y":0.47819767425900706,"w":0.70370371500651041,"t":"a family. The resulting work signifies a dramatic change in Moore's style, away from the","h":0.017441860778592888},{"x":0.090534987186456889,"w":0.72633743286132812,"t":"experimentation of the 1930s towards a more natural and humanistic subject matter. He did","c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.49558303882791477},{"x":0.088477374629368347,"y":0.51148409913353288,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"w":0.77777776082356775,"t":"dozens of studies in clay for the sculpture, and these were cast in bronze and issued in editions of"},{"t":"seven to nine copies each. In this way, Moore's work became available to collectors all over the","h":0.021134036168613979,"c":1,"w":0.7594736735026042,"x":0.086317593727724212,"y":0.52552791620880246},{"w":0.75524144490559897,"x":0.08843098490223042,"t":"world. The boost to his income enabled him to take on ambitious projects and start working on","h":0.016615111639698976,"y":0.54494917173553914,"c":1},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.088477371645347205,"c":1,"y":0.56242638384582,"t":"the scale he felt his sculpture demanded.","w":0.32510286966959639},{"t":"Critics who had begun to think that Moore had become less revolutionary were proven wrong","w":0.74691360473632817,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.088477353869220399,"c":1,"y":0.59593023242476106},{"y":0.6104293101160162,"h":0.018811647125351993,"x":0.088432267656614744,"t":"by the appearance, in 1950, of the first of Moore's series of standing figures in bronze, with their","c":1,"w":0.77170013427734385},{"y":0.62926972888208588,"t":"harsh and angular pierced forms and distinct impression of menace. Moore also varied his subject","x":0.086419760515379668,"w":0.78395060221354151,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1},{"y":0.645348837062934,"h":0.016017476296396826,"c":1,"w":0.77572016398111965,"t":"matter in the 1950s with such works as Warrior with Shield and Falling Warrior. These were rare","x":0.086419753289192255},{"t":"examples of Moore's use of the male figure and owe something to his visit to Greece in 1951,","x":0.088395149879458845,"c":1,"y":0.66004534995989605,"h":0.020229269955548523,"w":0.74915410359700518},{"w":0.46728622436523443,"c":1,"x":0.088381862467678943,"t":"when he had the opportunity to study ancient works of art.","y":0.67833339455166275,"h":0.017825009825653604},{"t":"In his final years, Moore created the Henry Moore Foundation to promote art appreciation and","y":0.71220930216646028,"w":0.75308639526367194,"h":0.017472676590558955,"x":0.088477378396970605,"c":1},{"y":0.72965116265808039,"t":"to display his work. Moore was the first modern English sculptor to achieve international critical","x":0.086419745137485321,"c":1,"w":0.77366256713867188,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"acclaim and he is still regarded as one of the most important sculptors of the 20th century.","w":0.71810699462890626,"y":0.74558303881387944,"x":0.090534979913888758,"c":1},{"x":0.84567901245819177,"y":0.92005813935786906,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"59","c":1,"w":0.024691357612609877}],"w":2400}